WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:04.600
Enough theory.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.340
Let's generate a real Chenile service, build it, and call it.

3
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.130
And watch the definition and

4
00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.550
implementation split appear on disk.

5
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.640
You need four things:

6
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.780
Java 17 or later, Maven, git, and a shell.

7
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.180
jgen is pure Java

8
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.630
— no Node required.

9
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.930
The old app-gen generator is deprecated.

10
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.600
One-time setup:

11
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.870
clone chenile-gen, run make, and source setpath.

12
00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.020
That puts jgen on your PATH.

13
00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:34.910
Run jgen, pick the chenile-service blueprint,

14
00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.680
name it orders, and say yes to JPA.

15
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:38.620
There it is:

16
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.710
orders-api and orders-service.

17
00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.010
The exact split from last episode

18
00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.660
— generated for you.

19
00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:46.920
A service is a library.

20
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.360
To run it, generate a mini-monolith

21
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.340
— ordersdeploy

22
00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.900
— and add orders as a dependency.

23
00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.490
Build the service, then the deployable, and start it.

24
00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:59.230
Call the generated endpoint with the curl script

25
00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:00.960
— and there's the response.

26
00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:04.860
Business logic, a health probe, and an HTTP binding.

27
00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.240
And we wrote none of the plumbing.

28
00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.250
Look at the implementation again:

29
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.760
still just business logic.

30
00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.330
Everything else came from the framework.

31
00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:14.850
Next episode:

32
00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.480
we start adding the horizontal behavior

33
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:18.670
— as policies.
